            <div xml:id="d742">

                <pb facs="0973" n="871" xml:id="pg871"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">765.84/2870: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Consul at Geneva</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Gilbert</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1935-12-04T19:00:00-05:00">December 4, 1935—7
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>144. Your 638, December 4, 2 p.m. Do not make an appointment with Vasconcellos
                    concerning this matter. As soon as any opportunity presents itself, however, you
                    should, after talking with the Minister make clear to Vasconcellos the substance
                    of the Department’s 141 and previous telegrams concerning our policy. Similar
                    clarification should be made in your discretion to other officials whenever
                    opportunity and occasion offers.</p>
                <p>It is almost incomprehensible that any misunderstanding should still exist in any
                    quarter in Geneva concerning our position, which has repeatedly been stated in
                    definite and unambiguous terms.</p>
                <p>Please keep the Minister informed of any conversations you may have along these
                    lines.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
